{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01H7ptMzcZYAZ9WZZcDfFVC9","type":"tool_result","content":"1603\t=== WRITE C:\\dev\\lodestar\\certcomp\\..\\Book-KCNA/knowledge-base/concepts/absent-component-pattern.md ===\n1604\t# Concept — The absent-component pattern\n1605\t\n1606\t**Naming home:** Ch 3 §4 (where the name is coined)\n1607\t**Full treatment:** Ch 10 §3 and Ch 10 §8 (Zenith) · **two further instances at Ch 11 §3 and §5**\n1608\t**B3 cross-cutting theme:** #3 — retrieved *by name* at Ch 13 §7 and Ch 17 §7\n1609\t**Status:** ⚑ **TWO CONFLICTS OPEN — canonical form, and instance count.**\n1610\t**⛔ DO NOT DRAFT Ch 13 §7 OR Ch 17 §7 UNTIL THE COUNT IS RESOLVED.**\n1611\t\n1612\t---\n1613\t\n1614\t## The rule\n1615\t\n1616\t> **An object without its component does nothing.**\n1617\t\n1618\tVerbatim from shipped Ch 3 §4; reproduced verbatim in Ch 10 §3, Ch 10 §8, and Ch 11's Voyage\n1619\tAhead. **Do not paraphrase this sentence in any chapter** — it is retrieved as a quotation.\n1620\t\n1621\tCh 10 §8's compression, which later chapters should reach for:\n1622\t\n1623\t> An object is a record of intent. Intent does not act.\n1624\t\n1625\t## ⚑ CONFLICT 1 — canonical form (carried from Ch 10's Stage 14)\n1626\t\n1627\t| Form | Where it lives | Verdict |\n1628\t|---|---|---|\n1629\t| **\"the absent-component pattern\"** | Shipped Ch 3 §4, reader-facing ×4 | **Recommended headword** |\n1630\t| \"an object without its component does nothing\" | Shipped Ch 3 §4; Ch 10 ×9; Ch 11 ×3 | The **rule sentence**. Not a name. |\n1631\t| \"The object exists; nothing happens without the component\" | B7 ledger only | **Zero occurrences in shipped text.** Do not adopt. |\n1632\t| \"Nothing Happens Without a Controller\" | Ch 10 §8 heading | A section title, not a term |\n1633\t\n1634\t**Recommendation:** headword = *the absent-component pattern* (naming home Ch 3 §4); rule\n1635\tsentence as above; instance ledger owned by Ch 10 §3.\n1636\t\n1637\t## ⚑ CONFLICT 2 — the instance count. **NEW at Ch 11. This is the blocking one.**\n1638\t\n1639\t**Two incompatible counting conventions are now in shipped and finalized text.**\n1640\t\n1641\t### Convention A — Chapter 10's, and it is graded\n1642\t\n1643\t`chapter-10:634` has the reader at three by Ch 10 §3, and `chapter-10:1567` — Practice Q18's\n1644\t**correct answer** — enumerates four by Ch 10 §7:\n1645\t\n1646\t1. `type: LoadBalancer` Service with no provider — **Ch 9 §3**\n1647\t2. Service whose selector matches no Pods — **Ch 9 §4**\n1648\t3. Ingress with no Ingress controller — **Ch 10 §3**\n1649\t4. NetworkPolicy on a plugin that does not implement NetworkPolicy — **Ch 10 §7** (the only\n1650\t   silent one)\n1651\t\n1652\t`chapter-10:1795` marks option B — which names only Ch 10's two instances — wrong, with this\n1653\trationale: *\"the common error here is **undercounting**, not misnaming.\"*\n1654\t\n1655\t### Convention B — Chapter 11's, which restarts at the Ingress\n1656\t\n1657\t- `draft-v2.md:587` — *\"This is the **third** sighting\"*: Ingress, NetworkPolicy, StorageClass\n1658\t- `draft-v2.md:889` — *\"three times in three sections: an Ingress without a controller, a\n1659\t  StorageClass without a provisioner, and now this. Here is **the fourth**\"*\n1660\t- `draft-v2.md:1402` — *\"the Ingress controller, the network plugin, the provisioner, and the\n1661\t  CSI driver — **four sightings**\"*\n1662\t\n1663\t**Chapter 11 drops both Chapter 9 instances** — the exact undercount Ch 10 grades as wrong.\n1664\tA reader who answered Ch 10 Q18 correctly is told six pages later that the StorageClass is\n1665\tthe third; by the count they were graded on, it is the fifth.\n1666\t\n1667\t**`draft-v2.md:889` is also internally inconsistent**: its own three-item list already\n1668\tincludes the current (CSI) case, and the sentence then announces \"the fourth.\" It silently\n1669\tdrops the NetworkPolicy instance that line 587 included two sections earlier. **The two\n1670\tenumerations inside Chapter 11 are not the same set.**\n1671\t\n1672\t### Why this blocks Ch 13 and Ch 17\n1673\t\n1674\tCh 10's Stage 14 shard reserved instance **#5 for Ch 13 §7** (`kubectl top` with no\n1675\tmetrics-server) and **#6 for Ch 17 §7** (VPA as an addon). Chapter 11 has inserted two\n1676\tinstances and renumbered from a different origin. **The conventions now diverge by exactly\n1677\ttwo**, and whichever ordinal Ch 13 uses contradicts a graded item in the other chapter.\n1678\t\n1679\t### Recommendation\n1680\t\n1681\t1. Amend Ch 11 §3/§5/Voyage Ahead to continue Convention A (StorageClass = fifth, CSI =\n1682\t   sixth). Faithful to graded canon; the ordinals get clumsy.\n1683\t2. **Preferred: stop numbering instances in prose.** Keep the rule and the enumeration, drop\n1684\t   the ordinal. Ch 10 already had to reconcile two counts in a dedicated paragraph\n1685\t   (`chapter-10:625`); Ch 11 is the third count, and the reconciliation cost now exceeds the\n1686\t   rhetorical benefit. **The list transfers; the number breaks.**\n1687\t\n1688\tEither way, `draft-v2.md:889`'s internal contradiction needs fixing regardless.\n1689\t\n1690\t**This shard deliberately does not pick a winner.** Both conventions are recorded above so\n1691\tno drafting stage can adopt one without seeing the other.\n1692\t\n1693\t## The instance ledger (Convention A ordering, origin Ch 9 §3)\n1694\t\n1695\t| # | Instance | Where | Announces itself? |\n1696\t|---|---|---|---|\n1697\t| 1 | `type: LoadBalancer` Service, no provider | Ch 9 §3 | Yes — `<pending>` |\n1698\t| 2 | Service whose selector matches no Pods | Ch 9 §4 | Yes — traffic fails |\n1699\t| 3 | Ingress with no Ingress controller | Ch 10 §3 | Yes — requests fail loudly |\n1700\t| 4 | NetworkPolicy on a plugin that does not implement it | Ch 10 §7 | **No — silent** |\n1701\t| 5 | **StorageClass naming a provisioner nobody deployed** | **Ch 11 §3** | Yes — claim unbound, Pod `Pending` |\n1702\t| 6 | **StorageClass naming a CSI driver never installed** | **Ch 11 §5** | Yes — same signature |\n1703\t| 7 | `kubectl top` with no metrics-server | Ch 13 §7 (planned) | Yes — command errors |\n1704\t| 8 | VPA, an addon not shipped by default | Ch 17 §7 (planned) | Yes |\n1705\t\n1706\t*Rows 5–6 are Ch 11's \"third\" and \"fourth\" under Convention B. Rows 7–8 were #5 and #6 in\n1707\tCh 10's shard and have shifted.*\n1708\t\n1709\t**Instances 5 and 6 are the same failure at two depths** — a StorageClass whose provisioner\n1710\tis a CSI driver nobody deployed *is* both — which is an argument for the un-numbered\n1711\ttreatment. Ch 11 §5's sources state it as a plain ordering requirement rather than a warning:\n1712\t*\"To use a CSI driver from a storage provider, you must **first** deploy it to your cluster,\"*\n1713\tand *\"the core of Kubernetes does not install that software for you.\"*\n1714\t\n1715\t## The asymmetry — provenance, keep the split\n1716\t\n1717\tInstances 1–3 and 5–8 announce themselves. **Instance 4 does not.** The plugin dependency and\n1718\tthe \"no effect\" consequence are **documented**\n1719\t`[source: k8s-docs-network-policies-depth-2026-08-24]`. The characterisation of that failure\n1720\tas *silent* is **the book's own inference**, labelled as one in Ch 10 §7. Do not promote it.\n1721\t\n1722\t## The transferable question\n1723\t\n1724\t> **What is watching this, and is it installed?**\n1725\t\n1726\tCh 10 §8 hands this to the reader; Ch 11 §5 restates it as *\"you stop asking 'is the object\n1727\tthere?' and start asking 'is the **component** there?'\"* Ch 13 §7 and Ch 17 §7 should invoke\n1728\tit in these words.\n1729\t\n1730\t## Constraints on later chapters\n1731\t\n1732\t- Ch 13 §7 and Ch 17 §7: retrieve **by name**; do not re-derive. **Blocked on Conflict 2.**\n1733\t- Any chapter adding an instance: extend the table, do not restate the rule.\n1734\t- **Never illustrate an instance as a broken or blocked object.** Every genuine instance is a\n1735\t  **correct** object with nothing wrong with it. Ch 10 Practice Q18 option D is built on that\n1736\t  distinction (a mismatched `pathType` is a manifest bug, not an instance), and Ch 11 §3's\n1737\t  framing depends on it too: *\"`kubectl get` shows it, `kubectl describe` shows a sensible\n1738\t  spec, and nothing happens.\"*\n1739\t=== END WRITE ===\n1740\t\n1741\t=== WRITE C:\\dev\\lodestar\\certcomp\\..\\Book-KCNA/knowledge-base/objective-coverage.md ===\n1742\t# Objective Coverage — KCNA"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8899959a-2d32-4641-ba38-45cae6a1cb65","uuid":"6c790fcd-f054-42f3-a922-ac87250850ee","timestamp":"2026-08-31T07:58:21.049Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\.pipeline-state\\ch-11\\kb-manifest.md","content":"=== WRITE C:\\dev\\lodestar\\certcomp\\..\\Book-KCNA/knowledge-base/concepts/absent-component-pattern.md ===\n# Concept — The absent-component pattern\n\n**Naming home:** Ch 3 §4 (where the name is coined)\n**Full treatment:** Ch 10 §3 and Ch 10 §8 (Zenith) · **two further instances at Ch 11 §3 and §5**\n**B3 cross-cutting theme:** #3 — retrieved *by name* at Ch 13 §7 and Ch 17 §7\n**Status:** ⚑ **TWO CONFLICTS OPEN — canonical form, and instance count.**\n**⛔ DO NOT DRAFT Ch 13 §7 OR Ch 17 §7 UNTIL THE COUNT IS RESOLVED.**\n\n---\n\n## The rule\n\n> **An object without its component does nothing.**\n\nVerbatim from shipped Ch 3 §4; reproduced verbatim in Ch 10 §3, Ch 10 §8, and Ch 11's Voyage\nAhead. **Do not paraphrase this sentence in any chapter** — it is retrieved as a quotation.\n\nCh 10 §8's compression, which later chapters should reach for:\n\n> An object is a record of intent. Intent does not act.\n\n## ⚑ CONFLICT 1 — canonical form (carried from Ch 10's Stage 14)\n\n| Form | Where it lives | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|\n| **\"the absent-component pattern\"** | Shipped Ch 3 §4, reader-facing ×4 | **Recommended headword** |\n| \"an object without its component does nothing\" | Shipped Ch 3 §4; Ch 10 ×9; Ch 11 ×3 | The **rule sentence**. Not a name. |\n| \"The object exists; nothing happens without the component\" | B7 ledger only | **Zero occurrences in shipped text.** Do not adopt. |\n| \"Nothing Happens Without a Controller\" | Ch 10 §8 heading | A section title, not a term |\n\n**Recommendation:** headword = *the absent-component pattern* (naming home Ch 3 §4); rule\nsentence as above; instance ledger owned by Ch 10 §3.\n\n## ⚑ CONFLICT 2 — the instance count. **NEW at Ch 11. This is the blocking one.**\n\n**Two incompatible counting conventions are now in shipped and finalized text.**\n\n### Convention A — Chapter 10's, and it is graded\n\n`chapter-10:634` has the reader at three by Ch 10 §3, and `chapter-10:1567` — Practice Q18's\n**correct answer** — enumerates four by Ch 10 §7:\n\n1. `type: LoadBalancer` Service with no provider — **Ch 9 §3**\n2. Service whose selector matches no Pods — **Ch 9 §4**\n3. Ingress with no Ingress controller — **Ch 10 §3**\n4. NetworkPolicy on a plugin that does not implement NetworkPolicy — **Ch 10 §7** (the only\n   silent one)\n\n`chapter-10:1795` marks option B — which names only Ch 10's two instances — wrong, with this\nrationale: *\"the common error here is **undercounting**, not misnaming.\"*\n\n### Convention B — Chapter 11's, which restarts at the Ingress\n\n- `draft-v2.md:587` — *\"This is the **third** sighting\"*: Ingress, NetworkPolicy, StorageClass\n- `draft-v2.md:889` — *\"three times in three sections: an Ingress without a controller, a\n  StorageClass without a provisioner, and now this. Here is **the fourth**\"*\n- `draft-v2.md:1402` — *\"the Ingress controller, the network plugin, the provisioner, and the\n  CSI driver — **four sightings**\"*\n\n**Chapter 11 drops both Chapter 9 instances** — the exact undercount Ch 10 grades as wrong.\nA reader who answered Ch 10 Q18 correctly is told six pages later that the StorageClass is\nthe third; by the count they were graded on, it is the fifth.\n\n**`draft-v2.md:889` is also internally inconsistent**: its own three-item list already\nincludes the current (CSI) case, and the sentence then announces \"the fourth.\" It silently\ndrops the NetworkPolicy instance that line 587 included two sections earlier. **The two\nenumerations inside Chapter 11 are not the same set.**\n\n### Why this blocks Ch 13 and Ch 17\n\nCh 10's Stage 14 shard reserved instance **#5 for Ch 13 §7** (`kubectl top` with no\nmetrics-server) and **#6 for Ch 17 §7** (VPA as an addon). Chapter 11 has inserted two\ninstances and renumbered from a different origin. **The conventions now diverge by exactly\ntwo**, and whichever ordinal Ch 13 uses contradicts a graded item in the other chapter.\n\n### Recommendation\n\n1. Amend Ch 11 §3/§5/Voyage Ahead to continue Convention A (StorageClass = fifth, CSI =\n   sixth). Faithful to graded canon; the ordinals get clumsy.\n2. **Preferred: stop numbering instances in prose.** Keep the rule and the enumeration, drop\n   the ordinal. Ch 10 already had to reconcile two counts in a dedicated paragraph\n   (`chapter-10:625`); Ch 11 is the third count, and the reconciliation cost now exceeds the\n   rhetorical benefit. **The list transfers; the number breaks.**\n\nEither way, `draft-v2.md:889`'s internal contradiction needs fixing regardless.\n\n**This shard deliberately does not pick a winner.** Both conventions are recorded above so\nno drafting stage can adopt one without seeing the other.\n\n## The instance ledger (Convention A ordering, origin Ch 9 §3)\n\n| # | Instance | Where | Announces itself? |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `type: LoadBalancer` Service, no provider | Ch 9 §3 | Yes — `<pending>` |\n| 2 | Service whose selector matches no Pods | Ch 9 §4 | Yes — traffic fails |\n| 3 | Ingress with no Ingress controller | Ch 10 §3 | Yes — requests fail loudly |\n| 4 | NetworkPolicy on a plugin that does not implement it | Ch 10 §7 | **No — silent** |\n| 5 | **StorageClass naming a provisioner nobody deployed** | **Ch 11 §3** | Yes — claim unbound, Pod `Pending` |\n| 6 | **StorageClass naming a CSI driver never installed** | **Ch 11 §5** | Yes — same signature |\n| 7 | `kubectl top` with no metrics-server | Ch 13 §7 (planned) | Yes — command errors |\n| 8 | VPA, an addon not shipped by default | Ch 17 §7 (planned) | Yes |\n\n*Rows 5–6 are Ch 11's \"third\" and \"fourth\" under Convention B. Rows 7–8 were #5 and #6 in\nCh 10's shard and have shifted.*\n\n**Instances 5 and 6 are the same failure at two depths** — a StorageClass whose provisioner\nis a CSI driver nobody deployed *is* both — which is an argument for the un-numbered\ntreatment. Ch 11 §5's sources state it as a plain ordering requirement rather than a warning:\n*\"To use a CSI driver from a storage provider, you must **first** deploy it to your cluster,\"*\nand *\"the core of Kubernetes does not install that software for you.\"*\n\n## The asymmetry — provenance, keep the split\n\nInstances 1–3 and 5–8 announce themselves. **Instance 4 does not.** The plugin dependency and\nthe \"no effect\" consequence are **documented**\n`[source: k8s-docs-network-policies-depth-2026-08-24]`. The characterisation of that failure\nas *silent* is **the book's own inference**, labelled as one in Ch 10 §7. Do not promote it.\n\n## The transferable question\n\n> **What is watching this, and is it installed?**\n\nCh 10 §8 hands this to the reader; Ch 11 §5 restates it as *\"you stop asking 'is the object\nthere?' and start asking 'is the **component** there?'\"* Ch 13 §7 and Ch 17 §7 should invoke\nit in these words.\n\n## Constraints on later chapters\n\n- Ch 13 §7 and Ch 17 §7: retrieve **by name**; do not re-derive. **Blocked on Conflict 2.**\n- Any chapter adding an instance: extend the table, do not restate the rule.\n- **Never illustrate an instance as a broken or blocked object.** Every genuine instance is a\n  **correct** object with nothing wrong with it. Ch 10 Practice Q18 option D is built on that\n  distinction (a mismatched `pathType` is a manifest bug, not an instance), and Ch 11 §3's\n  framing depends on it too: *\"`kubectl get` shows it, `kubectl describe` shows a sensible\n  spec, and nothing happens.\"*\n=== END WRITE ===\n\n=== WRITE C:\\dev\\lodestar\\certcomp\\..\\Book-KCNA/knowledge-base/objective-coverage.md ===\n# Objective Coverage — KCNA","numLines":140,"startLine":1603,"totalLines":2002}}}
