{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Cr8s33grammkbDQC1akKDG","type":"tool_result","content":"1099:A closing note for the next chapter: a Pod that references a Secret which does not exist does not get a running container. The kubelet cannot assemble the container's configuration, so the container sits waiting rather than starting and crashing — a recognizably different shape from a Pod that runs and then dies, and one of the first things to check when a Pod never comes up. *[cross-bearing: see Ch 13 §2 — pods that never start]*\n1101:[Omitted long matching line]\n1340:A Pod refused by `enforce` **never starts**. It is not a Pod that starts and crashes; it is an object the API server declined to accept. That is a different diagnostic shape from anything in the crash-loop family, and it shows up at a different point in the triage flow. *[cross-bearing: see Ch 13 §2 — pods that never start]*"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8899959a-2d32-4641-ba38-45cae6a1cb65","uuid":"3edf0987-22d8-42ec-96f2-e61944dc76a2","timestamp":"2026-08-31T08:00:18.871Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"1099:A closing note for the next chapter: a Pod that references a Secret which does not exist does not get a running container. The kubelet cannot assemble the container's configuration, so the container sits waiting rather than starting and crashing — a recognizably different shape from a Pod that runs and then dies, and one of the first things to check when a Pod never comes up. *[cross-bearing: see Ch 13 §2 — pods that never start]*\n1101:[Omitted long matching line]\n1340:A Pod refused by `enforce` **never starts**. It is not a Pod that starts and crashes; it is an object the API server declined to accept. That is a different diagnostic shape from anything in the crash-loop family, and it shows up at a different point in the triage flow. *[cross-bearing: see Ch 13 §2 — pods that never start]*","numLines":3,"totalLines":3}}
