{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MUehH1zr4YsnJZ7TuEJ1rt","type":"tool_result","content":"509:**6.** *[retrieval: ch2]* You want a Pod to run one exact, unchangeable build of an image, with no possibility that a moved pointer silently gives you different content. Do you reference the image by tag or by digest, and why?\n561:**6. B.** *[retrieval: ch2]*\n897:**6.** *[retrieval: ch5]* A Pod has one container that requests 500m CPU and 512Mi memory, with limits of 500m CPU and 512Mi memory. What QoS class is it, and why?\n949:**6. B.** *[retrieval: ch5]*\n1139:**2.** *[retrieval: ch8]* Your control plane is at 1.37. You are asked whether a node running kubelet 1.33 is supported. What is the answer, and what is the rule?\n1146:**3.** *[retrieval: ch10]* Which of the following best describes what an HPA does on a cluster with no metrics-server installed?\n1180:**2. B.** *[retrieval: ch8]*\n1188:**3. C.** *[retrieval: ch10]*\n1337:**2.** *[interleaved: D1.3 scheduling]* A Pod has been in `Pending` for fifteen minutes. `kubectl describe pod` shows a scheduler event reporting that all six nodes in the cluster were rejected because each carried a taint the Pod does not tolerate. What is the correct interpretation?\n1381:**8.** *[interleaved: D1.1 workloads]* A Deployment shows `ProgressDeadlineExceeded` and has zero available replicas. `kubectl describe deployment` gives you the condition but no cause. What is the correct next step?\n1388:**9.** *[interleaved: D2.2 security]* A Pod will not start. Its container reports `CreateContainerConfigError`, and the Pod spec mounts a Secret named `db-credentials` as a volume. `kubectl get secret db-credentials` returns `NotFound`. What is the diagnosis, and at what stage did it fail?"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8899959a-2d32-4641-ba38-45cae6a1cb65","uuid":"c6fa38ec-8f38-4782-92ab-16043ea5686b","timestamp":"2026-08-31T08:04:12.445Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"509:**6.** *[retrieval: ch2]* You want a Pod to run one exact, unchangeable build of an image, with no possibility that a moved pointer silently gives you different content. Do you reference the image by tag or by digest, and why?\n561:**6. B.** *[retrieval: ch2]*\n897:**6.** *[retrieval: ch5]* A Pod has one container that requests 500m CPU and 512Mi memory, with limits of 500m CPU and 512Mi memory. What QoS class is it, and why?\n949:**6. B.** *[retrieval: ch5]*\n1139:**2.** *[retrieval: ch8]* Your control plane is at 1.37. You are asked whether a node running kubelet 1.33 is supported. What is the answer, and what is the rule?\n1146:**3.** *[retrieval: ch10]* Which of the following best describes what an HPA does on a cluster with no metrics-server installed?\n1180:**2. B.** *[retrieval: ch8]*\n1188:**3. C.** *[retrieval: ch10]*\n1337:**2.** *[interleaved: D1.3 scheduling]* A Pod has been in `Pending` for fifteen minutes. `kubectl describe pod` shows a scheduler event reporting that all six nodes in the cluster were rejected because each carried a taint the Pod does not tolerate. What is the correct interpretation?\n1381:**8.** *[interleaved: D1.1 workloads]* A Deployment shows `ProgressDeadlineExceeded` and has zero available replicas. `kubectl describe deployment` gives you the condition but no cause. What is the correct next step?\n1388:**9.** *[interleaved: D2.2 security]* A Pod will not start. Its container reports `CreateContainerConfigError`, and the Pod spec mounts a Secret named `db-credentials` as a volume. `kubectl get secret db-credentials` returns `NotFound`. What is the diagnosis, and at what stage did it fail?","numLines":11,"totalLines":11}}
